      <span class="eff">Docs · no account needed</span>
      <h1>How GitLaunch works</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        GitLaunch is a deployment dashboard that sits on top of the CI you already run.
        It is not another CI/CD tool. The whole integration is two HTTP calls, documented
        below in full — read them, run them, or read the source. Nothing here needs
        an account.
      </p>

      <div class="tldr">
        <h2>In one breath</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your CI <strong>POSTs a build</strong> to GitLaunch when it goes green.</li>
          <li>Someone on your team clicks <strong>Deploy</strong> (or calls the API); GitLaunch <strong>triggers your CI</strong> to deploy that exact build to an environment.</li>
          <li>Your deploy job <strong>PATCHes its status</strong> back. The dashboard shows what is live where, and lets anyone roll back.</li>
          <li>Open core: <a href="{{sourceUrl}}">the source is on GitHub</a> and you can self-host it for free on one account.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

